      "why": "Two armored blocks, R5C3 and R4C6, and nothing that can ever hit them where it stands. The only hammer is the purple clockwise spinner at R6C4, and two magnets carry it. The blue magnet at R5C4 sits right above it: when the magnet leaves upward it first turns the spinner (it is a neighbour) and then drags it into R5C4 - so the spinner arrives facing left, at the first shell, only if it was turned exactly twice before, by both of its other neighbours (P at R6C3 and B at R7C4, freed by the spinner Y at R7C3). Ram; the cracked red block leaves downward and turns the hammer to face up. Now the green magnet at R5C6 drags it along row 5 to R5C6, right under the second shell: ram again; the cracked yellow block leaves to the right and turns the hammer to face right, out. Every departure re-aims the same hammer. Checked over every winning line (56): the hammer is aimed by a magnet's escape and carried by both magnets in every one, the blue magnet always fires at step 5, before the green one; only 2 of the 3 legal first moves keep the board solvable.",
